 "source_type": "instagram",
 "source_url": "https://www.instagram.com/reel/Df381xpg-km/",
 "title": "Make Scripted Content Sound Natural",
 "topic": "content creation",
 "summary": "The creator explains their technique for making word-for-word scripted content sound natural while reading off a screen. By breaking the script down line by line and determining intent and emotion before speaking, they achieve a conversational pace and tone.",
 "key_points": [
  "Write the script line by line.",
  "Before saying a line, read it once in your head and ask what the line is trying to mean.",
  "Ask how the line should feel (e.g., excited, sad, or surprised).",
  "Look away from the laptop, look straight at the camera, and say the line naturally.",
  "Pause, look back at the laptop, and do the same with the next line.",
  "Do this for every line of the script instead of trying to read the whole thing in one go.",
  "Pauses are cut out in editing so they are never seen by viewers.",
  "Reading one sentence at a time gives natural pace so it feels like talking to the camera rather than reading a screen."
 ],
 "content": "Post text: How I Make Scripted content sound Natural. Transcript: Yes all my content is scripted, word for word, but how do I still sound so natural if I'm reading off of a screen? I'll tell you how and it's way simpler than you think. I have my laptop right here, where my script is written line by line. Then, before I say a line, I do two things. First, I read one line in my head and ask, 'What is this line trying to say?' Second, I ask, 'How should it feel? Excited? Sad? Surprised?' Once I know that, I look away from the screen, look straight at the camera, and say it like I would naturally say something. Then I pause, look back at the laptop, and do the same with the next line. I do this for every line of the script, not every word. I never try to read the whole thing in one go. Just one sentence at a time. The pauses get cut out in the edit, so nobody ever sees them. So it feels like I'm talking to you in my room, but I'm actually reading off a script. This is exactly how I got to 74,000 followers in just 7 months. That's it. Follow me for more. Text shown on screen: How I Make Scripted content sound Natural, Yes all my scripted, word for word, but how do I, still sound, so natural, even if I'm, reading off of a screen, I'll tell you how, and it's way, simpler than you think, I have my laptop, where my script is written line by line, Then, before I say a line, I do two things. First, I read one line in my head and ask, 'What is this line trying to say?', Second, I ask, 'How should it feel? Excited? Sad? Surprised?', Once I know that, I look away from the screen, look straight at the camera, and say it like I would naturally say something., Then I pause, look back at the laptop, and do the same with the next line., I do this for every line of the script, not every word. I never try to read the whole thing in one go. Just one sentence at a time. The pauses get cut out in the edit, so nobody ever sees them., So it feels like I'm talking to you in my room, but I'm actually reading off a script., This is exactly how I got to 74,000 followers in just 7 months. That's it. Follow me for more., 100000 followers combined.",
